+# EVM / wallet compatibility in Falcon mode
+
+Falcon mode changes **only** QBFT consensus signatures: messages and COMMIT seals.
+- EVM transaction signing, account addresses, `ecrecover`, JSON-RPC and MetaMask stay secp256k1 ECDSA.
+- Tested: a legacy EIP-155 tx (v=0x1bda9e for chainId 912701) was included with status 1, and its `from` matched the sender (`logs/ecdsa-compat-1.log`).
+- Tested: 20 000 ECDSA load txs, all included (`logs/perf-*.log`).
+- **Not tested:** EIP-1559 (type-2) and EIP-2930 (type-1) txs, and a real MetaMask UI session.
+- Falcon-signed user transactions were **not implemented**. The owner cancelled that work at 12:43 JST on 2026-11-03. A prototype precompile was reverted, and its patch is archived in `logs/falcon-tx-cancelled.patch`.
