+# PQ authentication across L1 / AI / P2P / VPS — design (not deployed)
+
+Status: **design only**. Nothing here was applied to chain 9127, the VPS or production services.
+
+| Layer | Today | PQ design | Algorithm |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| L1 consensus (912701 test net) | Falcon-1024 seals + ML-DSA-65 finality cert | as implemented here | Falcon-1024 (round-3 BC) + ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204) |
+| L1 consensus (9127 prod) | ECDSA QBFT + ML-DSA-65 finality cert | unchanged until owner approval (see README rollout) | — |
+| EVM accounts / wallets | secp256k1 ECDSA (MetaMask) | **unchanged** | ECDSA |
+| AI agents / services → API | bearer tokens | Challenge–response: the service issues a nonce, and the agent signs `ZERONYTH/AUTH/V1 ‖ service ‖ nonce ‖ expiry` with ML-DSA-65. The service verifies the signature against a registry of agent public keys; the registry entries are themselves signed by an ML-DSA root key. Tokens are short-lived (≤15 min) and bound to the key id. | ML-DSA-65 |
+| P2P (devp2p RLPx) | secp256k1 ECIES handshake | Keep RLPx. Add an application-level PQ attestation of the node identity: a Falcon `PQ_BINDING` from enode key to validator. A full PQ transport (ML-KEM-768 hybrid with X25519) requires a devp2p fork, so it is deferred. | ML-KEM-768 hybrid (future) |
+| VPS admin access | SSH password/key | Move to OpenSSH `sntrup761x25519` / `mlkem768x25519` KEX (OpenSSH ≥9.9) with key-only login. Disable passwords after owner approval. Store the ML-DSA-signed host-key fingerprint list in the repo. | ML-KEM hybrid KEX |
+
+Common rules:
+- Every signature carries a domain string, a chain/service id, a purpose and an expiry. Messages are never signed raw.
+- Keys are stored encrypted with 0600 permissions, one key per purpose, and rotated with the same add-then-remove pattern used for validators.
+- Verification has no network trust: verifiers pin roots (genesis hash, ML-DSA root key).
+
+## Local verification API (implemented, 127.0.0.1:18780, test net only)
+- `GET /v1/info`: chain, genesis and trust model.
+- `GET /v1/verify/block/<n|latest>`: verifies Falcon seals and quorum against the vote-tally validator set, plus the ML-DSA-65 finality certificate.
+  Returns `VERIFIED`, or `FALCON_VERIFIED_PQ_FINALITY_NOT_VERIFIED`, or `FAILED` / `NOT_CONNECTED`. It never reports success for unverified data.
+- `POST /v1/verify/falcon` `{publicKey (raw 1792 B hex), message, signature}`: raw Falcon-1024 verification (round-3) plus the derived address.
+- `POST /v1/verify/envelope` `{envelope, chainId, type, height, round, payloadHash, allowed?}`: verifies a ZQBF envelope (chainId is required).
+- `POST /v1/verify/mldsa65` `{publicKey, message, signature}`: ML-DSA-65 verification.
