+# Validator-set transition bug (found and fixed in test-net tooling)
+
+**QBFT semantics:**
+- Block N's `extraData.validators` is the set that seals block N. It already includes the votes of blocks ≤ N−1.
+- The votes in block N (coinbase = proposer, ADD 0xff / DROP empty) only take effect from block N+1. They apply once ≥ floor(n/2)+1 distinct proposers have voted for the same subject.
+- Epoch blocks reset all pending votes.
+
+**Bug:** the explorer, the explorer server, the ML-DSA attester and the vendored light-client all took the *next* set from block N's extraData. After the 5→4 removal, the browser sync failed at block 2927 ("quorum 3/4 of 5").
+
+**Fix:**
+- `ValidatorTracker` in `falcon-verify-core.mjs` replays the votes exactly as Besu's `VoteTally` does.
+- Every verifier checks extraData validators against the tracked set, and quorum is computed from the tracked set.
+- Full replay of 0..4006: 12 101 seals, 0 failures, with transitions at 2863, 2927, 3009 and 3028. The wrong set for 2927 is rejected.
+- A second explorer bug was fixed at the same time:
+  - Overlapping browser sync passes applied votes twice and could overwrite FAILED with VERIFIED.
+  - The fix is a re-entrancy guard; FAILED is now terminal.
+
+**Latent issue (NOT changed, production-adjacent):** `tools/vendor/light-client.mjs` (copied from the 9127 tooling) still uses `nextValidators: e.validators`. On 9127 it is harmless while the validator set never changes. The production light client should get the same tally logic before any validator vote on 9127. Changing it needs the owner's approval.
